{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The spectral ordering (NetworkX "},{"code":"spectral_ordering","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; Barnard, Pothen and Simon): the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components in order of their least vertex index; a component of at most two vertices in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index order; a larger one ascending by the Fiedler vector of that component (for a connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph, "},{"code":"fiedlerVector()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s), entries within 10⁻⁸ · max|x| of their predecessor kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index order. "},{"code":"[]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the empty graph."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"spectralOrdering"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"normalized"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":" = false, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8) -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"] "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","text":"BinaryInteger"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"normalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Traps when the work limit is spent: 4,000 + 20√n products on σI − L (then shift-invert),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1,000 shift-invert products, 20,000 + 2n per solve. Only a tolerance below rounding has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached it in the measurements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every weight is finite and nonnegative.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE16spectralOrdering6weight10normalized9toleranceSay6VertexQzGqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_SbSdtSzRd__lF","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector.swift#L286","fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift"},"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"title":"spectralOrdering(weight:normalized:tolerance:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spectralOrdering","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typ